I see this on p.238 of the manual:
If Sigma is a variable of type matrix, then Sigma[1] denotes the first row of Sigma and has the type row_vector.
So this suggests that you can do something like this:

real[rows(Y)] X;
for (i in 1:rows(Y))
  X[i] <- sum(Y[i]);

