Anyway, I was suggesting removing base_rng__ argument and initializing a new base_rng_ inside the c++ function.  The cost of initializing a new rng should not be a concern.  And users still can control the seed in R by doing something as follows (generate a seed form R's RNG).

boost::ecuyer1988 base_rng__(floor(R::runif(0, 1) * 0x7FFFFFFF));

Jiqiang

