Not sure where to direct feedback to, I'll just post it here: love it. Huge code-saver, especially for exploratory analysis. Some suggestions for further improvement (it's great already! I don't know where to check and see whether these suggestions have been given before):
Option to change the number of decimals in the output. Some of my models have rather badly behaved posteriors that require stepsizes <0.01 for the HMC algorithm to work well. Currently, I can't interpret the HMC diagnostics, as stepsizes <0.01 (or <0.005, I'm not sure) are printed as "0.00" (two decimals only).
Color legends for the chains in the trace plots (so I can link them with the chain HMC stats.
Density plots overlaid for different chains (currently I can only see one chain at a time, or the result of all chains in sequence).

Other than that: love it!

Best,

Luc

